<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Transamund II of Spoleto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 724 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Transamund II was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spoleto">Spoleto</a> from 724 who acted almost as an independent ruler. He allied with Pope Gregory III and the Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benevento">Benevento</a> against King Liutprand, who deposed him in 739; he regained the duchy in 740 but was finally overthrown in 742 and forced to become a cleric. His career shows the conflict between the Lombard kings and the southern duchies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/transamund-ii-of-spoleto.jpg" alt="Transamund II of Spoleto" width="320" height="364" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Il_duca_Faroaldo_che_nomina_erede_Trasmondo_(rilievo,_opera_isolata)_-_bottega_Italia_centrale_(sec._XVIII).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
